# Line endings are load-bearing here.
#
# Reproducible builds require byte-identical source on every platform. If a
# Windows checkout has CRLF and a Linux CI checkout has LF, the two builds
# produce different output hashes — and the whole verification story collapses
# before it starts. Force LF everywhere, in the repo and in working trees.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.wasm binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary

# Signatures and hashes must not be altered in any way
*.asc    binary
*.sig    binary
*.sha256 binary

# Approved UI handoff snapshots are immutable evidence. Preserve the exact
# maintainer-supplied bytes so their recorded hashes survive every checkout.
*.html.reference binary

# Vault files should never be committed, but if one ever is, don't corrupt it
*.cbx binary

# Diff hints
*.md   diff=markdown
*.json diff=json
